{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-013",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 13,
  "title": "Job 13",
  "display_title": "Job 13",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 13,
  "sortOrder": 18013,
  "verseCount": 28,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Lo, mine eye hath seen all this, mine ear hath heard and understood it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "What ye know, the same do I know also: I am not inferior unto you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Surely I would speak to the Almighty, and I desire to reason with God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But ye are forgers of lies, ye are all physicians of no value.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "O that ye would altogether hold your peace! and it should be your wisdom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Hear now my reasoning, and hearken to the pleadings of my lips.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Will ye speak wickedly for God? and talk deceitfully for him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Will ye accept his person? will ye contend for God?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Is it good that he should search you out? or as one man mocketh another, do ye so mock him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He will surely reprove you, if ye do secretly accept persons.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Shall not his excellency make you afraid? and his dread fall upon you?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Your remembrances are like unto ashes, your bodies to bodies of clay.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Hold your peace, let me alone, that I may speak, and let come on me what will.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Wherefore do I take my flesh in my teeth, and put my life in mine hand?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Though he slay me, yet will I trust in him: but I will maintain mine own ways before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "He also shall be my salvation: for an hypocrite shall not come before him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Hear diligently my speech, and my declaration with your ears.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Behold now, I have ordered my cause; I know that I shall be justified.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Who is he that will plead with me? for now, if I hold my tongue, I shall give up the ghost.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Only do not two things unto me: then will I not hide myself from thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Withdraw thine hand far from me: and let not thy dread make me afraid.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Then call thou, and I will answer: or let me speak, and answer thou me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "How many are mine iniquities and sins? make me to know my transgression and my sin.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and holdest me for thine enemy?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Wilt thou break a leaf driven to and fro? and wilt thou pursue the dry stubble?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "For thou writest bitter things against me, and makest me to possess the iniquities of my youth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Thou puttest my feet also in the stocks, and lookest narrowly unto all my paths; thou settest a print upon the heels of my feet.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:13:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "And he, as a rotten thing, consumeth, as a garment that is moth eaten.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 13:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:13:28"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
